    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T07:05:10Z",
    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main d911f4553. No code change is necessary.\n\nEvidence:\n\n- PR #2904 (#917) replaced the truck STEP importer with the solidcore kernel. Commit 776ba8b76 deleted `step_fit.rs`, `step_refine.rs` and the edge bisection of #2600. The surface fit that this issue names is not in the code now.\n- On d911f4553, `bar_cross_holes.step` imports with 33,546 facets. Before, the #2600 fit gave about 133,000 facets.\n- `the_step_bars_wall_facet_normals_follow_the_cylinder` prints `wall facets 31470 of 33546, normal over 25 degrees off the radius: 0, worst 1.8`. It runs in 0.51 s in a debug build. Before, the import took about 5 s.\n- `the_step_bars_wall_facets_lie_on_the_cylinder` passes: no wall facet edge is more than 0.02 mm inside the cylinder.\n- `a_gap_over_the_cap_is_refused_and_tight_fixtures_stay_full_fidelity` passes: the bar keeps full fidelity (`coarse_mm == None`, no \"reduced accuracy\" note). Verify does not refuse it.\n\nReadings: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test tilted_gouge` (4 passed) and `--test import_step_edge_gap` (3 passed), on a clean worktree of d911f4553.\n\nSuggest closing as already done by PR #2904. The maintainer decides.\n",
